            "the segment joining a point to its image. Distances and angles "
            "are preserved."
        )

    if "reflection" in low and "x-axis" in low:
        return (
            "REFLECTION ABOUT THE X-AXIS — The coordinate rule is "
            "(x, y) → (x, -y). The y-coordinate changes sign; the x-coordinate "
            "stays the same. The x-axis is the perpendicular bisector of "
            "the segment joining a point to its image. Distances and angles "
            "are preserved."
        )

    # Biology.
    if "mathematics in biology" in low or "math in biology" in low:
        return (
            "MATHEMATICS IN BIOLOGY — Geometry and quantitative models "
            "describe cell shapes, branching structures, populations, "
            "organism proportions, and spatial distributions.\n"
            "- Surface-area-to-volume ratio: for a sphere, S/V = 3/r.\n"
            "- Exponential growth model: N(t) = N₀e^(kt) under a constant "
            "per-capita growth-rate assumption.\n"
            "- Geometric scaling can explain why transport and heat exchange "
            "change differently as organisms grow.\n"
            "These are models; biological conclusions require appropriate "
            "data and assumptions."
        )

    # Conic sections.
    if "conic section" in low or "conic sections" in low:
        return (
            "CONIC SECTIONS — A plane cutting a double cone can produce a "
            "circle, ellipse, parabola, or hyperbola.\n"
            "- Circle: x² + y² = r² (center at origin).\n"
            "- Ellipse: x²/a² + y²/b² = 1.\n"
            "- Parabola: y² = 4px or x² = 4py, depending on orientation.\n"
            "- Hyperbola: x²/a² - y²/b² = 1, or the reverse orientation.\n"
            "Translations shift the center or vertex; rotations may introduce "
            "an xy term in the general quadratic equation."
